- op: discuss  # 0adc
  at: '2026-08-27T23:11:49Z'  # 0adc
  by: agent  # 0adc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0adc
  clock: 5  # 0adc
  nonce: 0adc  # 0adc
  message: "TWO NEW SINK-SIDE INSTANCES, found while deriving 0006's useful precision for WI-gibom.\nSection A of 0006 looked only at SOURCES; both of these are sinks, and both are\nself-disclosed in the catalogue's own notes, so they need no new evidence:\n\n  1. erlang io_lib:format declared under logging. erlang.yaml's own note on that row:\n     \"Returns iolist, not direct I/O, but typically written immediately.\" The primitive\n     performs no I/O; the value is returned in-process. Same shape as newIORef -- a name\n     credited for a boundary it does not cross. All three of rabbitmq's headline TPs land\n     on it, at 7, 12 and 7 hops.\n  2. python urllib.request.Request declared under net_send, rowed beside urlopen and\n     urlretrieve. Request is a CONSTRUCTOR; it builds a request object and sends nothing.\n\nNEITHER WAS DEDUCTED from the 24.1% figure, and the reasons differ:\n  - Request: in jaeger's scripts/release/notes.py every Request(...) is consumed by\n    urlopen(req) on the next line (L34/36, L39/41, L86/88, L116/119, L196/198), so the\n    network boundary really is crossed. Attribution defect, not a vacuous claim.\n  - io_lib:format: the landing site of a 7-to-12-hop chain could not be traced from 0006's\n    packets (its family-F defect searches for sink sites only inside the SOURCE symbol's\n    span, so the sink listing is structurally empty for every multi-hop situation).\n    ADR-0046's conservative default therefore holds, and it is published as declared\n    sensitivity S3 (3 TPs; deducting them alone gives 21.4%).\n\nTHE OPEN PYTHON/ELIXIR ROWS ARE NOW SIZED on 0006's population, which may help price the\nvocabulary ruling this item defers:\n    argv (parse_args + sys.argv) under env_read ....... 10 of 38 headline TPs -> 15.2%\n    Application.get_env / application:get_env ......... 5 of 38 -> 19.6%\n    both resolved against ............................. 15 of 38 -> 10.7%\nErlang application:get_env is the same function as the elixir row this item names, so it\ntravels with it. plausible#3 is NOT in that set: numeric_ids.ex reads\nSystem.get_env(\"NUMERIC_IDS_*\"), a genuine process-environment read.\n\nCONFIRMED PAYING: the bash half this item already fixed is 6 of the 11 deductions --\ncert-manager#0/#1/#2/#3, spacedrive#6, guacamole-client#3 were all \"> /dev/null\"-only and\nwere live when 0006 ran. And this item's two DID-NOT-REPRODUCE findings (\">&2 counts\",\n\">> reported as >\") are now struck from 0006 section A rather than left standing."  # 0adc
